# Trivy misconfiguration suppressions for this repo (intentional, documented).

# AVD-DS-0002 — the worker image builds on the shared worker-bridge base,
# which runs as root by design today (same as aws-s3-bucket): the runtime user
# is governed by the agent's worker pod securityContext, not by a USER
# directive here. Revisit when the bridge ships a non-root variant.
AVD-DS-0002

# AVD-AZU-0012 — the storage account's network rule uses
# default_action = "Allow" (bypass: AzureServices) on purpose. Linked
# applications reach the blob endpoint over the public internet and authorise
# with the per-link SAS; setting this to "Deny" would cut them off, since
# private endpoints and network ACLs are out of scope for this version.
# Access still requires a valid SAS and public blob access is disabled
# (allow_nested_items_to_be_public = false). See "The account is reachable
# from the public internet" in the README. Flagged for product review.
AVD-AZU-0012
